# samples/05-EfCrud – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/05-EfCrud
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5105

### Scaffolded list – sorted, paged, only the allowlisted fields
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/products?sort=-price&page=1&pageSize=10

### Filters generated from the filterable fields
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/products?maxPrice=20&sort=name

### 400 – stock isn't sortable
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/products?sort=stock

### Create – "id" and "purchasePrice" are ignored (no mass assignment)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/shop/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "TNT-5", "name": "Dynamite", "price": 9.5, "stock": 100, "id": 999, "purchasePrice": 1 }

### 400 from the interceptor
POST {{baseUrl}}/shop/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "NEG-1", "name": "Debt", "price": -1, "stock": 1 }

### Patch – only the fields sent
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/{{created.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "TNT" }

### Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/{{created.response.body.id}}

### Get with its ETag
# @name product
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/1

### 428 – this endpoint requires If-Match
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 5 }

### 412 – a stale ETag
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "stale"

{ "stock": 5 }

### 200 – the current ETag (copy it from the get above if your client doesn't support response headers)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/shop/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{product.response.headers.ETag}}

{ "stock": 5 }

### Hand-written list with a contains filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/categories?q=ool

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/shop/categories/1

### The entities admins may use
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/crud/entities

### Scaffolding through the admin API – a dry run
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/scaffold/crud?entity=categories&routePrefix=/catalog/categories&dryRun=true
